ok 5 a symlinked dir that resolves to the sessions dir is denied
ok 6 a Bash write into the sessions dir is denied
ok 7 every Bash write shape against session state is denied
ok 8 any command but a reader that names a state path is denied
ok 9 a glob that matches the state file once ~ is expanded is denied
ok 10 plain reads, git commands and messages naming state or settings: no vote
ok 11 a shell reading a here-doc runs its body as commands
ok 12 a # that bash does not read as a comment hides no state write
ok 13 a misread << hides no state write
ok 14 a double-quoted state target is denied
ok 15 reads of a state file, and a commit message naming one: no vote
ok 16 the session id counts only as the state file name: scratchpad writes pass
ok 17 reads of session state: no vote
ok 18 a Monitor command writing the state file is denied
ok 19 a scheduled prompt or relayed message carrying /kern:autopilot is denied
ok 20 relayed text that opens with a mode or autopilot command is denied
ok 21 relayed text that only mentions a mode command: no vote
ok 22 a RemoteTrigger whose nested body carries a kern command is denied; a list passes
ok 23 a scheduled prompt without kern commands: no vote
ok 24 a Skill call to the mode or autopilot skill is denied; other skills pass
ok 25 a write to a kern settings file asks, and denies under autopilot
ok 26 reading a kern settings file: no vote
ok 27 a command that names neither state nor settings costs G16 no lower-casing; any case still counts
ok 28 a settings path spelled with ., .. or // or split by quotes is still a settings path
ok 29 a copy, move or link into a .claude directory is a settings write
ok 30 a write to Claude Code's own settings asks, and denies under autopilot; plain reads get no vote
ok 31 settings files and .claude directories follow the state model: any head but a reader asks
ok 32 git reads only through its read-only subcommands; any other git naming settings or .claude asks
ok 33 a settings write under a directory with a space asks; only a message option's text is read as a sentence
ok 34 a command that reads but can run code, and names a hook or state_set, asks; under autopilot it is denied
ok 35 a glob, brace or zsh group after hooks/ that could name a hook asks; under autopilot it is denied
ok 36 running, sourcing or reading a hook, or calling a state function, asks; under autopilot it is denied
ok 37 a hooks directory named elsewhere in the command, or reached by a glob, makes a hook's bare name ask
ok 38 a command that names no kern hook, such as a hook's test file, gets no hook vote
ok 39 inside a hooks directory a bare hook name, or a glob that could match one, asks
ok 40 when awk cannot read the command for kern's hook code, G16 fails closed
